<https://github.com/kieker-monitoring/kieker/pull/201/events/MDEOlBbGxSZXFZXNUmVaWVMTcMTYMDk> a prov:Activity ;
    github2prov:body """Either in addition or instead of the 'local-build.sh' script to execute the pipeline locally, we could also use a Docker-based solution to resemble the build as exact as possible (due to the unified environment with Docker).\r
\r
Here is a draft for a Docker variant:\r
\r
```\r
#!/usr/bin/env bash\r
\r
####\r
# This script allows to run the all tasks in the same environment as it is\r
# executed on the Kieker build server.\r
#\r
# Example:\r
# ./runLocalPipeline.sh\r
# This would execute all tasks that are also executed in the Jenkins pipeline.\r
#\r
#\r
# Requirements:\r
# - Docker\r
###\r
\r
# Check if user is in docker group\r
groups | grep docker >/dev/null\r
\r
if [ $? -eq 0 ]; then\r
  docker run -u `id -u` --rm -v `pwd`:/opt/kieker kieker/kieker-build:openjdk8 /bin/bash -c "\\\r
    cd /opt/kieker;\\\r
    ./gradlew clean && \\\r
    ./gradlew compileJava compileTestJava &&\\\r
    ./gradlew test &&\\\r
    ./gradlew check &&\\\r
    ./gradlew checkReleaseArchivesShort &&\\\r
    ./gradlew checkReleaseArchives"\r
else\r
  echo "You are not in the docker group."\r
fi\r
```"""^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <https://github.com/kieker-monitoring/kieker/commit/ae677beb181a1c7335d43bdd82d8e0b38a9a55ca> .

