<https://github.com/kieker-monitoring/kieker/pull/208/events/MDEOlBbGxSZXFZXNUmVaWVMTgNTMOTc> a prov:Activity ;
    github2prov:body "What is the reason for putting test classes into a separate `test` package? As far as I know it is generally accepted good practice to put test classes in the the same package as the class under test, but (as we already do) in a separate directory structure. For example, to be able to test package-private classes or methods. Unfortunately no better sources than [[1]](https://softwareengineering.stackexchange.com/questions/328780/naming-convention-for-test-packages), [[2]](https://stackoverflow.com/questions/811827/where-should-i-put-my-junit-tests), [[3]](http://www.kyleblaney.com/junit-best-practices/). I know, this is the convention in Kieker, but perhaps we should reconsider this practice."^^xsd:string ;
    prov:wasInformedBy <https://github.com/kieker-monitoring/kieker/commit/fadd3a43f4505e8bfb2758895cb5039a8bce7cb8> .

